      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "West Bengal is situated in eastern India, extending from the Himalayas in the north to the Bay of Bengal in the south.",
        "The state covers a total geographical area of 88,752 square kilometres.",
        "It shares international borders with three neighboring countries: Bangladesh, Bhutan, and Nepal.",
        "It shares domestic boundaries with five Indian states: Odisha, Jharkhand, Bihar, Sikkim, and Assam."
      ],
